<p>A brochure answers three questions: who you are, what you offer, and how to call. A catalogue answers a fourth: which product, at a price your own system already holds. A portal answers a fifth: a dealer, a staff member, or a customer logs in and sees a record that is not public. Those are different builds. A template can carry a brochure. It starts to fail when Arabic and English must stay in sync, when the price must come from a sheet the accountant trusts, or when a login has to hide one customer’s orders from another.</p>
